# AI AdTech Copilot

Pragmatic modular monolith under `src/`. No premature microservices.

## Separation of concerns

- UI (`src/components/` or `src/features/*/components`): presentation and interaction only.
- Data (`src/services/` or `src/features/*/services`): Supabase queries and mutations.
- AI (`src/lib/ai/`): Gemini calls, prompt formatting, and JSON parsing.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — query inside a component
const { data } = await supabase.from("campaigns").select("*");

// ✅ GOOD — component calls a service
const campaigns = await listCampaigns();
```

## Gemini

- Official Google AI SDK only. Key lives in `GEMINI_API_KEY`. Never hardcode it.
- Natural-language commands that become database actions must parse against a strict JSON schema.
- Keep system instructions short and in prompt modules, not inline in UI.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
const apiKey = process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY;
const action = CampaignActionSchema.parse(JSON.parse(raw));
```

## Typing and safety

- No `any`. Define interfaces for campaigns, logs, chat payloads, and API responses.
- Chat-triggered mutations must be idempotent (stable keys or upserts; no duplicate rows on retry).
- Wrap Supabase, Gemini, and other async work in `try/catch` and log through one error helper.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
catch (e) {}

// ✅ GOOD — plain words, file, and cause (see plain-english-errors)
catch (error) {
  logError({
    what: "Could not create the campaign.",
    why: "Supabase rejected the save.",
    file: "src/features/campaigns/services/create-campaign.ts",
    cause: error,
  });
  throw new CampaignMutationError("Could not create the campaign.", { cause: error });
}
```

## Layout

Group by feature under `src/features/<domain>/` (`components`, `services`, hooks) when a domain has more than one file.
